config.prompt:
The human wants you to propose the changes. Their note, which may be empty:

{{Node.Input}}

If the note names some of your proposals, or asks for changes to them, follow it; if it is empty, propose all of them. Then reply as your instructions say, ending with RETRO_DONE.

The human looked at the pull request and sent it back to you:

{{Node.Input}}

This is a decision and overrides the plan. Make the changes they ask for (read any comments they left on the pull request with get_pr_review), add or update tests and run them, commit, and end with READY_FOR_REVIEW or NEEDS_HUMAN.

New pull request activity:

{{Node.Input}}

Handle it as your instructions describe (get_pr_review for review items, get_ci_log for CI failures), commit your fixes, queue a reply for each comment, and end with READY_FOR_REVIEW or NEEDS_HUMAN.
